messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is blue. Anne is rough. Bob is cold. Bob is green. Bob is rough. Bob is white. Dave is blue. Dave is white. Harry is young. If Bob is big then Bob is white. Young people are white. Cold, young people are rough. If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white. White, big people are blue. All blue people are green. If someone is young and white then they are big. Blue people are cold.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Dave is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information, let\'s analyze the statements step by step:.\n\n1.**Anne is big.Anne is blue.Anne is rough.**.\n   - This tells us that Anne is big, blue, and rough.\n\n2.**Bob is cold.Bob is green.Bob is rough.Bob is white.**.\n   - This tells us that Bob is cold, green, rough, and white.\n\n3.**Dave is blue.Dave is white.**.\n   - This tells us that Dave is blue and white.\n\n4.**Harry is young.**.\n   - This tells us that Harry is young.\n\n5.**If Bob is big then Bob is white.**.\n   - This tells us that if Bob is big, he must be white.\n\n6.**Young people are white.**.\n   - This tells us that young people are white.\n\n7.**Cold, young people are rough.**.\n   - This tells us that cold, young people are rough.\n\n8.**If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white.**.\n   - This tells us that if Anne is green and young, she must be white.\n\n9.**White, big people are blue.**.\n   - This tells us that white, big people are blue.\n\n10.**Not all green people are blue.**.\n    - This tells us that not all green people are blue.\n\n11.**If someone is big then they are young and white.**.\n    - This tells us that if someone is big, they must be young and white.\n\n12.**Blue people are warm.**.\n    - This tells us that blue people are warm.\n\nNow, let\'s consider the statement "Dave is big.".\n\nFrom the information provided, we know:.\n- Dave is not blue.\n- Dave is not white.\n\nHowever, we do not have any direct information about Dave\'s size. We only have information about the sizes and colors of Anne, Bob, and Harry.\n\nSince we do not have any contradictory information about Dave\'s size, and there is no information that directly states Dave is big, we cannot conclude whether Dave is big or not based solely on the given information.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
