 sees the bald eagle.\n   - If something sees the bald eagle, then the bald eagle is young.\n   - Cold things are big.\n   - If something chases the tiger and it sees the cat, then the tiger is big.\n   - If something is big, then it chases the tiger.\n   - If something sees the bald eagle, then it sees the cat.\n\n2.**Statement Evaluation**:.\n   - The statement "The tiger chases the tiger" is a self-referential statement about the tiger\'s behavior towards itself.Based on the above information, the statement "The tiger chases the tiger" is true because the provided context clearly indicates that the tiger chases itself or another tiger.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
