ollows that Charlie must be big.However, we don\'t have any direct information about whether Charlie is smooth or not.We only know that all big people are rough (Statement 13), and all rough, furry people are cold (Statement 19).But this does not necessarily mean that all big people are furry.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, we cannot definitively conclude whether Charlie is smooth or not.The statement "Charlie is smooth" is unknown.\n\n<｜User｜>Based on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown?Charlie is smooth.\n# Options:.\nA) True.\nB) False.\nC) Unknown<｜Assistant｜>.\nBased on the given information, the statement "Charlie is smooth" is unknown.This is because the information provided does not explicitly state whether Charlie is smooth or not.While we know that Charlie is nice and nice people are big, and all big people are rough, and all rough, furry people are cold, we do not have enough information to determine if Charlie is smooth or not\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
