int 3).\n- Gary is furry (from point 4).\n\nSince Gary is not green and not white, according to point 6, Gary must be furry.However, we need to check if this furiness implies anything about Gary\'s coldness.\n\n- According to point 7, if someone is smart and furry, they are big.Since Gary is smart and furry, he must be big.\n- According to point 8, if someone is white and not cold, they are not blue.Since Gary is white and not blue, he must be cold.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, Gary is cold.\n\n<｜User｜>Based on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown?Gary is cold.\n# Options:.\nA) True.\nB) False.\nC) Unknown<｜Assistant｜>.\nBased on the given information, the statement "Gary is cold" is true.This conclusion is drawn from the following steps:.\n\n1.**Gary is smart**: This is directly stated in the context.\n2.**Gary is not green**: This is also directly stated in the context.\n3.**Gary is white**: This is directly stated in the context.\n4.**Gary is furry**: This is directly stated in the context.\n5.**All green people are furry**: This is a general rule.\n6.**If Gary is not green and Gary is not white then Gary is furry**: This is a conditional statement based on the previous information.\nGary is not cold.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
