l.\n   - If something needs the squirrel, it is green.\n   - If something is young, it needs the tiger.\n   - Green things are young.\n   - If something is big and it visits the lion, the lion needs the squirrel.\n   - If the squirrel is big and the squirrel does not like the tiger, the tiger is not big.\n\nBased on the indirect statement in the context, the squirrel visits the lion.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
