ishes a relationship between whiteness, niceness, and roughness.It does not directly relate to Harry\'s characteristics.\n\n6.**Furry, nice things are young.**.\n   - This statement suggests that if something is both furry and nice, it must be young.However, it does not provide information about Harry\'s characteristics.\n\n7.**Furry, young things are white.**.\n   - This statement indicates that if something is both furry and young, it must be white.Again, it does not provide information about Harry\'s characteristics.\n\n8.Based on the given information, we can confidently determine that the statement "Harry is big" is false. The analysis of the statements reveals that all big, blue things are white, and young, blue things are nice. This indirectly indicates that Harry is not big.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
